WEBVTT

00:00:00.772 --> 00:00:02.879
Previously on Supernatural

00:00:02.879 --> 00:00:03.983
Sammy.

00:00:03.983 --> 00:00:06.090
Take your brother outside
as fast as you can.

00:00:06.090 --> 00:00:07.795
Now Dean, go!

00:00:09.702 --> 00:00:11.407
Dad's on a hunting trip.

00:00:11.708 --> 00:00:14.016
And he hasn't been home in a few days.

00:00:14.718 --> 00:00:16.424
I swore I was done hunting.

00:00:16.424 --> 00:00:18.230
I can't do this alone.

00:00:18.732 --> 00:00:20.839
No! Jess!

00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:23.146
I think dad wants us to
pick up where he left off.

00:00:23.146 --> 00:00:25.354
You know, saving people. Hunting things.

00:00:25.354 --> 00:00:27.862
No. I got to find Jessica's killer.

00:01:29.769 --> 00:01:31.775
Be advised. We've found the victim.

00:01:34.384 --> 00:01:35.688
She's alive.

00:01:39.100 --> 00:01:40.705
It's okay. It's okay.

00:01:42.411 --> 00:01:44.016
In there.

00:01:47.127 --> 00:01:48.933
Let's go.

00:01:54.451 --> 00:01:55.555
Freeze!

00:01:55.755 --> 00:01:57.561
Don't move! Drop the knife!

00:01:57.561 --> 00:02:00.170
Keep your hands where
I can see them! Drop it.

00:02:00.170 --> 00:02:02.678
Hold it right there! Come on, come on!

00:02:02.678 --> 00:02:03.782
Now!

00:02:04.183 --> 00:02:05.789
Nice and easy!

00:02:06.591 --> 00:02:07.996
Do it!

00:02:27.762 --> 00:02:32.578
Alright, I figure we hit
Tucancary by lunch then head South.

00:02:32.578 --> 00:02:34.685
And best be by midnight.

00:02:36.190 --> 00:02:38.097
Sam wears women's underwear...

00:02:38.097 --> 00:02:39.501
I've been listening, I'm just busy.

00:02:39.501 --> 00:02:41.006
Busy doing what?

00:02:41.207 --> 00:02:42.712
Reading e-Mails.

00:02:44.518 --> 00:02:47.428
E-Mails from who? From
my friends at Stanford.

00:02:47.428 --> 00:02:50.739
You kidding? You still keep in
touch with your college buddies?

00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:52.444
Why not?

00:02:52.444 --> 00:02:53.448
Well...

00:02:57.060 --> 00:02:58.966
What do you exactly tell them?

00:02:59.167 --> 00:03:00.471
You know, about...

00:03:00.772 --> 00:03:02.077
Where you've been
What you've been doing.

00:03:02.077 --> 00:03:04.284
I tell them I'm on a road
trip with my big brother.

00:03:04.284 --> 00:03:07.294
I tell them I need some
time off after Jess.

00:03:07.294 --> 00:03:08.799
Oh, I see you lie to them?

00:03:08.799 --> 00:03:10.103
No.

00:03:10.103 --> 00:03:12.913
I just don't tell them everything.

00:03:12.913 --> 00:03:15.521
Yeah, dude. That's called lying.

00:03:15.521 --> 00:03:17.929
I mean, hey man. I get it. Telling
them the truth is far worse.

00:03:17.929 --> 00:03:21.341
So what am I suppose to do? Just
cut everybody out of my life?

00:03:22.043 --> 00:03:24.552
You're serious? Look, it sucks but...

00:03:24.552 --> 00:03:27.261
In a job like this you can't
get close to people, period.

00:03:27.261 --> 00:03:29.669
You're kind of
anti-Social, you know that?

00:03:29.669 --> 00:03:31.776
You know, whatever.

00:03:34.685 --> 00:03:36.993
God. What?

00:03:38.197 --> 00:03:41.809
This e-Mail from Rebecca Warren
one of those friends of mine.

00:03:41.809 --> 00:03:43.414
Is she hot?

00:03:43.615 --> 00:03:46.224
I went to school with
her and her brother Zach.

00:03:46.224 --> 00:03:48.732
She says, Zach's been
charged with murder.

00:03:48.732 --> 00:03:50.338
He's been arrested for
killing his girlfriend.

00:03:50.338 --> 00:03:53.649
Rebecca says he didn't do it but...

00:03:53.649 --> 00:03:56.458
Sounds like the cops
have a pretty good case.

00:03:56.458 --> 00:03:58.966
Dude, what kind of people
are you hanging out with?

00:03:58.966 --> 00:04:01.073
No man, I know Zach. He's no killer.

00:04:01.073 --> 00:04:04.184
Then maybe you know Zach
as well as he knows you.

00:04:04.184 --> 00:04:06.291
St. Louis, we're going.

00:04:06.893 --> 00:04:09.301
I'm sorry about you buddy, okay?

00:04:09.301 --> 00:04:11.408
But this doesn't sound
like our kind of problem.

00:04:11.408 --> 00:04:13.013
It is our problem. They're my friends.

00:04:13.013 --> 00:04:16.425
St. Louis is 400 miles behind us, Sam.

00:04:32.378 --> 00:04:35.287
Oh, my god! Sam! Well
if it isn't little Becky?

00:04:35.287 --> 00:04:37.997
You know you could do
that little Becky crap.

00:04:41.207 --> 00:04:44.819
I got your e-Mail. I didn't
think you would come here.

00:04:44.819 --> 00:04:46.625
Dean, older brother.

00:04:46.625 --> 00:04:48.331
Hi. Hi.

00:04:48.532 --> 00:04:49.736
We're here to help.

00:04:49.736 --> 00:04:51.441
Whatever we can do.

00:04:51.441 --> 00:04:52.846
Come in.

00:04:57.863 --> 00:05:00.371
Nice place. It's my parents.

00:05:00.371 --> 00:05:03.682
I was just crashing here for the
long weekend when everything happened.

00:05:03.682 --> 00:05:08.498
I decided to take this semester off.
I'm gonna stay until Zach's free.

00:05:08.498 --> 00:05:09.702
Where are your folks?

00:05:09.702 --> 00:05:11.408
They live in Paris for half the year

00:05:11.408 --> 00:05:14.217
So they're on their way
home now for the trial.

00:05:14.217 --> 00:05:16.224
Do you guys want a beer
or something? / Yeah...

00:05:16.224 --> 00:05:17.629
No, thanks.

00:05:18.231 --> 00:05:21.843
So, tell us what happened.

00:05:22.043 --> 00:05:23.749
Well...

00:05:23.950 --> 00:05:27.562
Zach came home and he
found Emily tied to a chair.

00:05:27.562 --> 00:05:32.679
And she was beaten up and bloody
and she wasn't breathing and so he

00:05:32.679 --> 00:05:36.692
He called 911 and the
police they showed up and..

00:05:36.793 --> 00:05:38.799
And they arrested him.

00:05:38.799 --> 00:05:41.107
But the thing is the only way that Zach

00:05:41.107 --> 00:05:45.823
Could have killed Emily if he was
in two places at the same time.

00:05:45.823 --> 00:05:47.528
The police they have a video.

00:05:47.528 --> 00:05:50.539
It's from the security
tape from across the street.

00:05:50.539 --> 00:05:55.355
And it shows Zach coming home at 10:30.

00:05:55.355 --> 00:05:57.662
Now, Emily was killed just after that

00:05:57.662 --> 00:06:00.171
But I swear he was here with me

00:06:00.171 --> 00:06:03.080
Having a few beers until
at least after midnight.

00:06:03.080 --> 00:06:06.291
You know, maybe we could see
the crime scene. Zach's house...

00:06:06.291 --> 00:06:08.097
We could.

00:06:08.799 --> 00:06:10.806
Why? I mean what could you do?

00:06:10.806 --> 00:06:15.422
Me? Not much but Dean's a cop.

00:06:18.030 --> 00:06:19.736
A detective actually.

00:06:19.736 --> 00:06:22.044
Really? Where?

00:06:22.044 --> 00:06:24.251
Bisbee Arizona.

00:06:25.154 --> 00:06:27.562
But I'm off duty now.

00:06:29.268 --> 00:06:33.582
You guys are so nice to
offer but I don't know...

00:06:33.582 --> 00:06:37.495
Beck, I know Zach didn't do this.

00:06:37.495 --> 00:06:42.512
Now, we have to find a way
to prove that he's innocent.

00:06:43.816 --> 00:06:45.321
Okay.

00:06:46.224 --> 00:06:48.933
I'm gonna go get the keys.

00:06:54.552 --> 00:06:57.161
Oh, yeah man. You're a real
straight shooter with your friends.

00:06:57.161 --> 00:06:58.465
Look...

00:06:58.465 --> 00:06:59.669
Zach and Becky need our help.

00:06:59.669 --> 00:07:01.375
I just don't think this
is our kind of problem.

00:07:01.375 --> 00:07:02.880
Two places at once?

00:07:02.880 --> 00:07:05.589
We've looked into less.

00:07:24.351 --> 00:07:26.157
You're sure this is okay?

00:07:26.157 --> 00:07:29.669
Yeah, I am an officer of the law.

00:07:46.826 --> 00:07:49.335
Beck, you want to wait outside?

00:07:50.238 --> 00:07:52.646
No, I wanna help.

00:08:00.472 --> 00:08:02.780
Tell us what else the police said.

00:08:02.780 --> 00:08:04.285
Well...

00:08:04.686 --> 00:08:06.592
There's no sign of a break in.

00:08:06.592 --> 00:08:09.000
They said Emily let her attacker in.

00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:13.014
And the lawyers, they're already
talking about plead bargain.

00:08:14.418 --> 00:08:16.224
Oh, god.

00:08:18.030 --> 00:08:19.435
Look, Beck.

00:08:19.435 --> 00:08:21.542
If Zach didn't do this

00:08:21.542 --> 00:08:24.352
It means somebody else did.

00:08:24.352 --> 00:08:26.358
And idea who?

00:08:29.669 --> 00:08:31.776
There was something.

00:08:31.776 --> 00:08:34.887
About a week before
somebody broke in here

00:08:34.887 --> 00:08:37.194
And stole some clothes.

00:08:37.194 --> 00:08:41.509
Zach's clothes. And the police
they don't think it's anything.

00:08:41.509 --> 00:08:44.920
We were not that far from downtown.

00:08:44.920 --> 00:08:47.730
Sometimes people get robbed.

00:08:55.957 --> 00:08:58.164
You know, that used
to be the sweetest dog.

00:08:58.164 --> 00:08:59.368
What happened?

00:08:59.368 --> 00:09:02.780
He just changed. You
remember when he changed?

00:09:02.780 --> 00:09:05.489
I guess around the time of the murder.

00:09:16.526 --> 00:09:18.031
Listen, the neighbor's dog went psycho

00:09:18.031 --> 00:09:21.342
Right around the time
Zach's girlfriend was killed.

00:09:21.542 --> 00:09:23.950
And most ??? Has a shock
since the paranormal.

00:09:23.950 --> 00:09:26.659
Yeah, maybe Fighto saw something.

00:09:27.462 --> 00:09:30.271
So, you think this is
our kind of problem?

00:09:30.271 --> 00:09:32.077
No, probably not.

00:09:32.077 --> 00:09:34.486
But we should look at the
security tape just to make sure.

00:09:34.486 --> 00:09:36.392
Yeah. Yeah.

00:09:38.499 --> 00:09:41.208
So, the tape. The security footage.

00:09:41.208 --> 00:09:42.613
You think maybe your lawyers
can get their hands on it.

00:09:42.613 --> 00:09:44.619
I just don't have that
kind of a jurisdiction..

00:09:44.619 --> 00:09:45.924
I've already got it.

00:09:45.924 --> 00:09:49.837
I don't want to say
something in front of the cop.

00:09:49.837 --> 00:09:52.044
I stole it off the lawyer's desk.

00:09:52.044 --> 00:09:54.552
I just had to see it for myself.

00:09:54.954 --> 00:09:56.459
Alright.

00:10:15.221 --> 00:10:16.726
I'll miss you.

00:10:17.730 --> 00:10:19.937
Why do they always have to send you?

00:10:19.937 --> 00:10:21.342
Because I'm the best.

00:10:21.342 --> 00:10:24.352
I know, that's why I
want you to stay home.

00:10:24.753 --> 00:10:26.860
It's just Kansas City.

00:10:27.462 --> 00:10:29.670
I'll be home tomorrow night

00:10:29.670 --> 00:10:31.375
And make it up to you.

00:10:35.890 --> 00:10:37.596
You better.

00:11:02.078 --> 00:11:03.683
Here he comes.

00:11:04.285 --> 00:11:06.994
22:04, that's just after 10.

00:11:06.994 --> 00:11:09.703
You said the time of
death is about 10:30.

00:11:09.703 --> 00:11:12.512
Our lawyers hired some
kind of video expert.

00:11:12.512 --> 00:11:14.720
He says the tapes are authentic.

00:11:14.720 --> 00:11:17.329
It wasn't tampered with.

00:11:20.539 --> 00:11:22.044
Hey, Beck.

00:11:22.044 --> 00:11:23.750
Can we take those beers now?

00:11:23.750 --> 00:11:25.355
Oh, sure.

00:11:26.559 --> 00:11:28.165
Hey...

00:11:28.466 --> 00:11:30.071
Maybe some sandwiches too?

00:11:30.071 --> 00:11:32.780
What do you think this, Hooters?

00:11:33.884 --> 00:11:35.690
I wish.

00:11:35.690 --> 00:11:38.198
What is it? Check this out.

00:11:45.623 --> 00:11:47.329
Maybe it's just a camera flare.

00:11:47.329 --> 00:11:49.737
That's not like any camera
flare I've ever seen.

00:11:49.737 --> 00:11:50.840
You know a lot of cultures believed

00:11:50.840 --> 00:11:53.148
That a photograph can catch
a glimpse of the soul. Right.

00:11:53.148 --> 00:11:54.553
You remember the dog
that was freaking out?

00:11:54.553 --> 00:11:55.857
Maybe he saw this thing.

00:11:55.857 --> 00:11:58.466
Maybe this is some kind
of dark double of Zach.

00:11:58.466 --> 00:11:59.870
It's something that looks
like him but isn't him.

00:11:59.870 --> 00:12:01.375
Like a Doppelganger? Yeah.

00:12:01.375 --> 00:12:04.586
That sure explains how he
was in two places at once.

00:12:13.717 --> 00:12:15.723
Honey, it's me.

00:12:17.630 --> 00:12:20.640
The client canceled at the last minute.

00:12:23.549 --> 00:12:26.359
I called, why didn't you answer?

00:12:29.871 --> 00:12:31.275
Lindsey?

00:12:33.884 --> 00:12:35.289
Lindsey?

00:12:38.901 --> 00:12:40.004
Lindsey?

00:12:45.723 --> 00:12:47.529
It's okay Lindsey. It's me.

00:12:47.529 --> 00:12:50.539
Please, don't hurt me anymore.

00:12:50.539 --> 00:12:52.546
Leave me alone.

00:13:51.643 --> 00:13:54.754
Alright. What are we doing
here at 5:30 in the morning?

00:13:54.754 --> 00:13:56.259
I realized something.

00:13:56.259 --> 00:13:59.670
The video tape shows the killer
going in but not coming out.

00:13:59.670 --> 00:14:01.576
So he came out the back door?

00:14:01.576 --> 00:14:04.085
Right. So there should
be a trail to follow.

00:14:04.085 --> 00:14:06.593
A trail the police will never pursue.

00:14:06.593 --> 00:14:10.306
Cause they think the killer never left
they caught your friend Zach inside.

00:14:10.306 --> 00:14:13.817
Still don't know what we're
doing here at 5:30 in the morning.

00:14:27.362 --> 00:14:29.168
Blood.

00:14:29.369 --> 00:14:31.075
Somebody came this way.

00:14:31.075 --> 00:14:34.687
Maybe the trail ends I
don't see anything over here.

00:14:52.045 --> 00:14:53.148
What happened?

00:14:53.148 --> 00:14:54.954
He tried to kill his wife.

00:14:54.954 --> 00:14:56.660
Tied her up and beat her.

00:14:56.660 --> 00:14:57.864
Really?

00:14:58.266 --> 00:15:02.279
I used to see him go to work in the
morning. He'd wave and say hello.

00:15:02.279 --> 00:15:04.888
He seemed like such a nice guy.

00:15:30.072 --> 00:15:31.175
Hey.

00:15:31.476 --> 00:15:33.684
Remember I said this isn't
our kind of problem? Yeah.

00:15:33.684 --> 00:15:35.791
It's definitely our kind of
problem. What did you find out?

00:15:35.791 --> 00:15:37.697
I just talked to the patrolmen
who was first in the scene.

00:15:37.697 --> 00:15:39.302
I heard this guy Alex's story.

00:15:39.302 --> 00:15:40.807
Apparently what he did was driving home

00:15:40.807 --> 00:15:42.714
From a business trip
when he was attacked.

00:15:42.714 --> 00:15:44.821
So he was at two
places at once. Exactly.

00:15:44.821 --> 00:15:47.931
Then he sees himself in the
house, police says he's a nut job.

00:15:47.931 --> 00:15:53.249
Two dark doubles attacking loved
ones in exactly the same way.

00:15:53.249 --> 00:15:55.858
Could be the same thing doing it too.

00:15:56.560 --> 00:15:58.065
Shape Shifter?

00:15:58.065 --> 00:15:59.771
Something that can make
itself look like anyone?

00:15:59.771 --> 00:16:02.379
Every culture in the world
has a Shape Shifter lure.

00:16:02.379 --> 00:16:05.590
The legends of creatures who can
transform itself into animals or other men.

00:16:05.590 --> 00:16:07.296
Right, skinwalkers, werewolves...

00:16:07.296 --> 00:16:09.202
We got two attacks from
them blocks from each other.

00:16:09.202 --> 00:16:12.714
I'm guessing we got a Shape
Shifter problem in the neighborhood.

00:16:12.714 --> 00:16:15.824
Let me ask you this. And
all this Shape Shifter lure.

00:16:15.824 --> 00:16:18.433
Can any of them fly?

00:16:19.135 --> 00:16:21.343
Not that I know of. I
picked up a trail here.

00:16:21.343 --> 00:16:24.453
Someone ran out of back of this
building, headed off this way.

00:16:24.453 --> 00:16:26.159
Just like you're friend's house. Yeah.

00:16:26.159 --> 00:16:30.874
And just like in Zach's
house the trail suddenly ends.

00:16:30.874 --> 00:16:32.881
Whatever it is It just...

00:16:32.881 --> 00:16:35.189
Disappeared.

00:16:36.192 --> 00:16:38.901
Well, there's another way to go.

00:16:38.901 --> 00:16:41.410
Down.

00:16:59.971 --> 00:17:03.182
I bet this runs right
by Zach's house too.

00:17:03.182 --> 00:17:06.694
The Shape Shifter can be using
the sewer system to get around.

00:17:06.694 --> 00:17:08.600
I think you're right.

00:17:09.403 --> 00:17:11.109
Look at this.

00:17:17.329 --> 00:17:20.841
Is this from his victims?

00:17:26.059 --> 00:17:27.865
You know I just had a sick thought.

00:17:27.865 --> 00:17:30.875
When the Shape Shifter changes shape...

00:17:31.176 --> 00:17:33.483
Maybe it sheds.

00:17:34.386 --> 00:17:36.393
That is sick.

00:17:37.296 --> 00:17:39.503
One thing I learned from dad.

00:17:39.503 --> 00:17:41.911
No matter what kind
of Shape Shifter it is.

00:17:41.911 --> 00:17:44.119
There's one sure way to kill it.

00:17:44.119 --> 00:17:47.229
Silver bullet to the
heart. That's right.

00:17:49.737 --> 00:17:51.744
This is Sam. Where are you?

00:17:51.744 --> 00:17:53.952
We're near Zach's. We're
just checking some things out.

00:17:53.952 --> 00:17:57.062
Well look Sam, just stop cause I
really don't need your help anymore.

00:17:57.062 --> 00:17:58.366
What are you talking about?

00:17:58.366 --> 00:18:01.276
I told the lawyers we
went to the crime scene.

00:18:01.477 --> 00:18:02.580
Why would you do that?

00:18:02.580 --> 00:18:04.487
I told them that we're
with a police officer

00:18:04.487 --> 00:18:08.500
And they checked it out and they told me
that there is no detective Dean Winchester.

00:18:08.500 --> 00:18:12.513
Beck... I don't understand why you would
lie to me about something like that.

00:18:12.614 --> 00:18:14.921
We're trying to help.
Oh, trying to help.

00:18:14.921 --> 00:18:17.330
Do you realize that that
was a sealed crime scene.

00:18:17.330 --> 00:18:18.835
This could have just ruined Zach's case.

00:18:18.835 --> 00:18:19.738
Beck, I'm sorry...

00:18:19.738 --> 00:18:21.544
No, goodbye Sam.

00:18:34.988 --> 00:18:38.400
I hate to say it but that's
exactly what I'm talking about.

00:18:38.400 --> 00:18:42.413
You lie to your friends because if they
know the real you they'd be freaked.

00:18:42.714 --> 00:18:44.019
It's just...

00:18:44.019 --> 00:18:46.728
It'll be easier... If I was like you.

00:18:46.728 --> 00:18:50.139
Hey, man. Like it or not.
We are not like other people.

00:18:50.440 --> 00:18:53.851
But I'll tell you one
thing. This whole gig.

00:18:55.356 --> 00:18:57.764
It ain't without purpose.

00:19:53.049 --> 00:19:54.855
I think we're close to its lair.

00:19:54.855 --> 00:19:55.959
Why do you say that?

00:19:55.959 --> 00:19:58.868
Cause there's another puking
dousing vile next to your face.

00:19:58.868 --> 00:20:00.373
Oh, god.

00:20:03.283 --> 00:20:05.089
Looks like he's lived here for a while.

00:20:05.089 --> 00:20:08.099
Who knows how many
murders he's got away with.

00:20:08.902 --> 00:20:10.206
Dean!

00:20:16.126 --> 00:20:18.333
Get the son of a bitch.

00:20:48.534 --> 00:20:50.039
Alright, let's split up.

00:20:50.039 --> 00:20:52.748
Alright, I'll meet you
around the inside. Alright.

00:21:30.072 --> 00:21:31.276
Hey.

00:21:33.885 --> 00:21:35.190
Anything?

00:21:35.190 --> 00:21:36.695
No, he's gone.

00:21:36.695 --> 00:21:38.701
Alright, let's get back to the car.

00:21:54.353 --> 00:21:57.062
You think he found
another way underground?

00:21:57.062 --> 00:21:58.467
Yeah, probably.

00:21:58.467 --> 00:22:00.273
You got the keys?

00:22:03.685 --> 00:22:08.400
Hey, didn't dad once face a
Shape Shifter in San Antonio?

00:22:08.400 --> 00:22:09.805
That was Auston.

00:22:09.805 --> 00:22:13.116
It didn't turn out to be a Shape
Shifter it was a Thought Form.

00:22:13.116 --> 00:22:16.026
A psychic projection, remember?

00:22:16.828 --> 00:22:18.434
Alright.

00:22:18.935 --> 00:22:20.942
Here you go.

00:22:36.996 --> 00:22:38.501
Don't move!

00:22:38.501 --> 00:22:40.106
What have you done with him?

00:22:40.106 --> 00:22:41.511
Dude, chill.

00:22:41.511 --> 00:22:43.517
It's me, alright? No, I don't think so.

00:22:43.517 --> 00:22:46.126
Where's my brother?
You're about to shoot him.

00:22:46.126 --> 00:22:48.634
Sam, calm down. You got
those keys with your left.

00:22:48.634 --> 00:22:49.939
Your shoulder was hurt.

00:22:49.939 --> 00:22:50.942
Yeah, it's better.

00:22:50.942 --> 00:22:52.146
What do you want me to do? Cry?

00:22:52.146 --> 00:22:54.153
You're not my brother.

00:22:55.758 --> 00:22:57.665
Won't you pull the trigger then?

00:22:57.665 --> 00:22:59.270
Cause you're not sure.

00:22:59.270 --> 00:23:00.875
Dude, you know me.

00:23:00.875 --> 00:23:02.380
Don't.

00:23:37.096 --> 00:23:39.003
Where is he?

00:23:39.504 --> 00:23:41.511
Where's Dean?

00:23:42.916 --> 00:23:45.324
I wouldn't worry about him.

00:23:45.825 --> 00:23:47.330
I would worry about you.

00:23:47.330 --> 00:23:49.036
Where is he?

00:23:50.441 --> 00:23:52.447
You don't really want to know.

00:23:54.554 --> 00:23:58.467
I swear the more I learn
about you and your family...

00:23:58.668 --> 00:24:01.578
I thought I came from a bad background.

00:24:01.578 --> 00:24:04.187
What do you mean learn?

00:24:24.855 --> 00:24:27.966
He sure got issues with you.

00:24:27.966 --> 00:24:30.575
You got to go to college.

00:24:30.575 --> 00:24:32.682
He had to stay home.

00:24:33.886 --> 00:24:36.695
I mean, I had to stay home. With dad.

00:24:36.695 --> 00:24:38.601
You don't think I had dreams of my own?

00:24:38.601 --> 00:24:40.608
But dad needed me.

00:24:40.809 --> 00:24:43.718
Where the hell were
you? Where is my brother?

00:24:43.718 --> 00:24:46.327
I'm your brother.

00:24:47.230 --> 00:24:49.638
You see, deep down...

00:24:49.638 --> 00:24:52.046
I'm just jealous.

00:24:52.046 --> 00:24:55.859
You got friends you can have a life.

00:24:56.361 --> 00:24:59.872
Me? I know I'm a freak.

00:24:59.872 --> 00:25:03.083
And sooner or later
everybody's gonna leave me.

00:25:04.889 --> 00:25:06.093
What are you talking about?

00:25:06.093 --> 00:25:08.100
You left.

00:25:08.100 --> 00:25:11.110
Hell, I did everything dad asked
me to and he ditched me too.

00:25:11.110 --> 00:25:14.220
No explanation, nothing. Just poof.

00:25:16.227 --> 00:25:19.337
Left me with your sorry ass.

00:25:23.150 --> 00:25:25.859
But still this life

00:25:25.859 --> 00:25:28.267
It's not without it's perch.

00:25:28.568 --> 00:25:31.779
I met the nicest people.

00:25:32.280 --> 00:25:33.986
Like little Becky.

00:25:33.986 --> 00:25:37.397
You know Dean would bang
her if he had the chance.

00:25:37.899 --> 00:25:40.207
Let's see what happens.

00:25:51.444 --> 00:25:52.949
Oh, hi.

00:25:52.949 --> 00:25:54.755
I know what you're
gonna say. Oh, you do.

00:25:54.755 --> 00:25:56.260
Well no, not exactly.

00:25:56.260 --> 00:25:58.267
But I could take a guess.

00:25:58.468 --> 00:26:00.575
Get off my porch.

00:26:01.177 --> 00:26:02.983
That's about right.

00:26:03.384 --> 00:26:07.397
I admit we lied thought
I tried to explain myself.

00:26:07.397 --> 00:26:09.003
Sam told me not to come but

00:26:09.003 --> 00:26:12.013
I thought what the hell I have to try.

00:26:18.033 --> 00:26:19.438
Damn it!

00:26:23.752 --> 00:26:27.063
That better be you Sam and
not that freaking nature.

00:26:27.464 --> 00:26:28.969
Yeah, it's me.

00:26:28.969 --> 00:26:32.080
He went to Becky's looking like you.

00:26:32.080 --> 00:26:34.187
Well, he's not stupid.

00:26:34.889 --> 00:26:37.097
He picked the handsome one.

00:26:42.214 --> 00:26:43.618
So, you're saying that

00:26:43.618 --> 00:26:48.434
There's something out there that
made itself look like my brother?

00:26:48.936 --> 00:26:51.946
What did you call it? The Shape Shifter.

00:26:52.849 --> 00:26:55.859
Yeah, maybe we're crazy.

00:26:55.859 --> 00:26:57.966
But what if we're not?

00:26:57.966 --> 00:27:01.277
I mean look, you said it yourself.
That Zach was in two places at once.

00:27:01.277 --> 00:27:04.689
Tell me how that can happen?
Okay, so... this thing.

00:27:04.689 --> 00:27:08.100
It can make itself look like anybody?

00:27:08.100 --> 00:27:09.605
That's right.

00:27:09.806 --> 00:27:11.210
What is it? Like a...

00:27:11.210 --> 00:27:13.418
Genetic freak?

00:27:15.123 --> 00:27:16.929
Maybe.

00:27:18.735 --> 00:27:21.043
Evolution is about mutation.

00:27:21.043 --> 00:27:22.950
Right?

00:27:22.950 --> 00:27:26.562
So, maybe this thing was born human

00:27:26.562 --> 00:27:28.970
But was different.

00:27:29.170 --> 00:27:32.582
Hideous and hated.

00:27:33.384 --> 00:27:36.796
Until he learned to become someone else.

00:27:41.010 --> 00:27:42.615
Yeah, that's the thing.

00:27:42.615 --> 00:27:45.324
He didn't just look like you he was you.

00:27:45.324 --> 00:27:47.933
Or at least becoming
you. What do you mean?

00:27:47.933 --> 00:27:51.946
I don't know, it was like he was
downloading your thoughts and memories.

00:27:52.047 --> 00:27:53.953
You mean, like the Volking Mindmill?

00:27:53.953 --> 00:27:55.458
Yeah, something like that.

00:27:55.458 --> 00:27:58.368
I mean, maybe that's why
it didn't just kill us.

00:28:01.679 --> 00:28:04.990
Maybe he needs to keep us alive.

00:28:05.291 --> 00:28:06.495
Psychic connection?

00:28:06.495 --> 00:28:07.699
Hands.

00:28:08.100 --> 00:28:09.103
Yeah.

00:28:09.103 --> 00:28:12.013
Go. We've got to go. He's
probably at Rebecca's already.

00:28:13.819 --> 00:28:16.829
Come on. We got to find
a phone call the police.

00:28:16.829 --> 00:28:20.542
Whoa, whoa, whoa. You're
gonna put an APB on me?

00:28:20.843 --> 00:28:22.147
Sorry.

00:28:22.548 --> 00:28:23.953
This way.

00:28:29.371 --> 00:28:30.876
It's funny.

00:28:31.679 --> 00:28:33.384
I kind of understand him.

00:28:33.384 --> 00:28:35.592
He's all alone.

00:28:36.394 --> 00:28:38.502
Close to no one.

00:28:38.502 --> 00:28:41.411
All he wants is for someone to love him.

00:28:44.221 --> 00:28:46.528
He's like me.

00:28:51.144 --> 00:28:53.351
Everybody needs...

00:28:53.351 --> 00:28:57.164
A little human touch now and then.

00:28:57.364 --> 00:28:59.271
It's so hard to be different.

00:28:59.271 --> 00:29:00.976
You should go.

00:29:09.104 --> 00:29:11.411
You are disgusting! Just
get the hell out of here!

00:29:11.411 --> 00:29:13.619
Rebecca, just calm down. I'll calm down!

00:29:13.619 --> 00:29:16.428
What is wrong with you?
What's wrong with me?

00:29:16.428 --> 00:29:17.632
What's wrong with you?

00:29:17.632 --> 00:29:19.538
I'm calling the police.

00:29:33.184 --> 00:29:34.689
Give me your hands!

00:29:35.492 --> 00:29:36.696
Shut up!

00:29:41.311 --> 00:29:43.719
You're a nice girl, Rebecca.

00:29:44.321 --> 00:29:46.127
I mean, I liked you.

00:29:47.833 --> 00:29:51.043
Believe me, it makes this harder.

00:29:54.154 --> 00:29:56.963
But I got to do what I got to do.

00:30:39.003 --> 00:30:40.107
Freeze!

00:30:40.308 --> 00:30:41.512
Call off the knife.

00:30:41.512 --> 00:30:42.917
Drop the knife!

00:30:43.117 --> 00:30:44.823
Drop the knife!

00:30:48.435 --> 00:30:49.639
Come on, come on.

00:30:50.141 --> 00:30:50.843
Go, go!

00:32:02.181 --> 00:32:05.392
An anonymous tip led police to
a home in the central west end

00:32:05.392 --> 00:32:08.903
Where a squad team discovered
a local woman found engaged.

00:32:08.903 --> 00:32:12.816
Her attacker a white male
approximately 24 to 30 years of age

00:32:12.816 --> 00:32:15.024
Was discovered hiding in the home.

00:32:15.024 --> 00:32:16.930
Shots were fired... Man!

00:32:17.131 --> 00:32:18.636
It's not even a good picture.

00:32:18.636 --> 00:32:20.141
It's good enough.

00:32:22.248 --> 00:32:23.452
Man.

00:32:27.766 --> 00:32:29.673
God. Come on!

00:32:32.281 --> 00:32:33.987
At least attempted
murder unless we know...

00:32:33.987 --> 00:32:35.392
I didn't kill her!

00:32:35.392 --> 00:32:37.298
I'm gonna check Rebecca in the
morning. See if she's alright.

00:32:37.298 --> 00:32:39.104
Alright, first I want to
find that handsome devil

00:32:39.104 --> 00:32:40.709
And kick the holy crap out of him.

00:32:40.709 --> 00:32:42.415
We have no weapons. No silver bullets.

00:32:42.415 --> 00:32:44.121
Man, the guy's walking
around with my face, okay?

00:32:44.121 --> 00:32:46.629
It's a little personal,
I want to find him.

00:32:47.332 --> 00:32:48.636
Okay.

00:32:48.636 --> 00:32:50.944
Where do we look? We can
start with the sewers.

00:32:50.944 --> 00:32:52.449
We have no weapons.

00:32:52.449 --> 00:32:55.057
He stole our guns. We need more.

00:32:57.064 --> 00:32:58.168
The car?

00:32:58.168 --> 00:32:59.572
I'm betting he drove
them over to Rebecca's.

00:32:59.572 --> 00:33:03.084
The news said he was on foot.
I bet it's still parked there.

00:33:03.385 --> 00:33:05.091
The thought of him driving my car!

00:33:05.091 --> 00:33:06.395
Oh, come on.

00:33:06.696 --> 00:33:08.703
But it's killing me! Let it go.

00:33:19.740 --> 00:33:21.445
There she is.

00:33:22.248 --> 00:33:24.756
Finally something right tonight.

00:33:27.566 --> 00:33:29.071
Oh, crap.

00:33:35.292 --> 00:33:36.596
This way, this way!

00:33:36.897 --> 00:33:37.900
You go, I'll hold them off.

00:33:37.900 --> 00:33:39.205
What are you talking
about? They'll catch you.

00:33:39.205 --> 00:33:40.308
Look, they can't hold me!

00:33:40.308 --> 00:33:43.419
Just go! Keep out of
sight! Meet me at Rebecca's.

00:33:43.619 --> 00:33:46.529
Dean! Stay out of the sewers alone!

00:33:46.930 --> 00:33:48.536
I mean it! Yeah, yeah!

00:33:48.536 --> 00:33:49.740
Don't move.

00:33:49.740 --> 00:33:52.248
Keep your hands where I can see them.

00:34:00.476 --> 00:34:02.181
I'm sorry Sam.

00:34:02.181 --> 00:34:03.987
You know me.

00:34:03.987 --> 00:34:05.793
I just can't wait.

00:34:43.218 --> 00:34:44.221
Rebecca?

00:34:44.221 --> 00:34:46.830
So, say the Shape Shifter is real.

00:34:46.830 --> 00:34:49.138
By the way you know you're crazy?

00:34:49.339 --> 00:34:52.449
But um.. Say it is real.

00:34:52.850 --> 00:34:54.656
How do you stop it?

00:34:54.656 --> 00:34:56.161
Thanks.

00:34:56.663 --> 00:34:58.870
Silver bullet to the heart.

00:34:59.874 --> 00:35:01.579
You are crazy.

00:35:04.790 --> 00:35:06.395
What happened?

00:35:06.596 --> 00:35:09.807
I was walking home and
everything just went white.

00:35:09.807 --> 00:35:10.710
Somebody hit me over the head

00:35:10.710 --> 00:35:14.623
And I rounded up just in time
to see that thing turn into me.

00:35:14.623 --> 00:35:17.031
How is that even possible? Okay, okay.

00:35:17.031 --> 00:35:18.034
It's okay.

00:35:18.034 --> 00:35:19.941
Come on. Can you walk?

00:35:19.941 --> 00:35:21.145
Okay, we've got to hurry.

00:35:21.145 --> 00:35:22.951
Sam went to see you.

00:35:31.579 --> 00:35:33.586
What are you gonna do to me?

00:35:33.887 --> 00:35:35.894
I'm not gonna do anything.

00:35:35.894 --> 00:35:37.800
Dean will though.

00:35:39.506 --> 00:35:40.911
You'll never catch him.

00:35:40.911 --> 00:35:43.118
Oh, it doesn't matter.

00:35:43.820 --> 00:35:46.730
Murder on the first his own brother.

00:35:46.730 --> 00:35:49.339
He'll be hunted the rest of his life.

00:35:54.656 --> 00:35:56.763
I must say,

00:35:56.763 --> 00:35:59.272
I will be sorry to lose this skin.

00:35:59.272 --> 00:36:02.282
Your brother's got a
lot of good qualities.

00:36:02.282 --> 00:36:05.392
You should appreciate more than you do.

00:36:06.195 --> 00:36:07.800
Cheers.

00:36:35.593 --> 00:36:37.198
You son of a bitch!

00:36:45.526 --> 00:36:46.931
Not bad, little brother.

00:36:46.931 --> 00:36:48.536
You're not him.

00:37:03.887 --> 00:37:05.794
Even when we were kids

00:37:05.794 --> 00:37:08.101
I always kicked your ass.

00:37:43.319 --> 00:37:44.623
Hey!

00:38:08.704 --> 00:38:10.108
Sam!

00:38:46.128 --> 00:38:47.734
So, this is what you do?

00:38:47.734 --> 00:38:51.546
You and your brother you hunt
down these kind of things.

00:38:51.546 --> 00:38:53.653
Yeah, pretty much. I can't believe it!

00:38:53.653 --> 00:38:56.864
I mean I saw with my own eyes and...

00:38:57.065 --> 00:38:58.771
Does everybody at school...

00:38:58.771 --> 00:39:01.078
Nobody knows that you do this?

00:39:01.078 --> 00:39:02.383
No.

00:39:02.684 --> 00:39:04.891
Did Jessica know?

00:39:05.894 --> 00:39:08.102
No, she didn't.

00:39:09.707 --> 00:39:11.513
Must be lonely.

00:39:11.513 --> 00:39:13.821
Oh, no. No, it's not that bad.

00:39:13.821 --> 00:39:17.031
Anyway what can I do? It's my family.

00:39:17.533 --> 00:39:20.041
Well you know Zach and me
and everybody at school.

00:39:20.041 --> 00:39:22.550
We really miss you.

00:39:23.453 --> 00:39:25.159
Yeah, me too.

00:39:28.369 --> 00:39:31.881
Well, will you call sometime?

00:39:32.182 --> 00:39:34.991
It might not be for a little while.

00:39:50.543 --> 00:39:52.751
So what about your friend Zach?

00:39:52.751 --> 00:39:57.466
Cops are blaming this Dean
Winchester guy for Emily's murder.

00:39:57.466 --> 00:39:59.774
They found the weapon in the guy's lair,

00:39:59.774 --> 00:40:02.383
Zach's clothes stained with her blood.

00:40:02.383 --> 00:40:05.794
Now they're thinking maybe the
surveillance tapes were tampered with.

00:40:05.794 --> 00:40:09.205
Yeah, Beck says Zach
would be released soon.

00:40:19.440 --> 00:40:20.945
Sorry man.

00:40:22.450 --> 00:40:24.356
About what?

00:40:25.460 --> 00:40:27.165
I really wish things could
be different, you know.

00:40:27.165 --> 00:40:29.172
I wish you could be

00:40:29.172 --> 00:40:31.580
Joe College. Na, that's okay.

00:40:32.182 --> 00:40:33.888
You know, the truth is...

00:40:33.888 --> 00:40:36.195
Even in Stanford deep
down I really never fit in.

00:40:36.195 --> 00:40:38.202
That's cause you're a freak.

00:40:38.202 --> 00:40:39.206
Yeah, thanks.

00:40:39.206 --> 00:40:41.112
I'm a freak too.

00:40:41.313 --> 00:40:43.721
I'm right there with you all the way.

00:40:44.724 --> 00:40:46.931
Yeah, I know you are.

00:40:48.035 --> 00:40:50.242
You know, I got to say.

00:40:50.443 --> 00:40:53.052
I'm sorry I'm gonna miss it. Miss what?

00:40:53.353 --> 00:40:56.664
How many chances am I gonna
have to see my own funeral?

00:00:00.571 --> 00:00:02.076
